; leashanchor.eval - a monster made in the editor or by `spawn` is leashed from
; its OWN square. Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 61, on its scratch world;
; `leashtest` is renamed to this worktree's save.
;
; Every monster carries a leash anchor: where a leashed one, pulled too far,
; breaks off and walks home to, and what its leash is measured from. Only the
; .ent loader set it (to the spawn square, or a record's leashfrom=); a monster
; built any other way - the editor's brush and the eval's `spawn` (AddMonster),
; a placed one put back by a save or a level re-entry (ApplyActiveSnapshot) -
; kept the struct's 0,0. A level saved then wrote `leashfrom=0,0` for it, and
; the editor's move tool, reading an anchor that was not the spawn as an
; authored one, left it on the corner for good. `leash` prints each monster's
; spawn, anchor and range.
;
;   --- checked ---   `validate` over the level files: the judge plants three
;                     leashed skeletons in crypt2.ent - anchored on the rock at
;                     0,0, off the map at 99,99, and on open floor at 6,6 (the
;                     control) - and the first two, only, are flagged.
;   --- made ---      a skeleton placed with the brush at 16,18 and one made by
;                     `spawn` at 20,18: each anchored on its own square.
;   --- moved ---     the placed one moved with the editor's move tool to
;                     14,18: its anchor goes with it.
;   --- returned ---  saved, then crypt1 and back: the two are rebuilt from the
;                     level's held state, each anchored on its own square.
;   --- loaded ---    the save loaded: the same.
;   --- leashed ---   the level's own six skeletons and the spawned one erased,
;                     so nothing else moves; the placed one given a leash of 1
;                     through its inspector, which saves the level.
;   --- shoved ---    the party at 15,18 facing it, a gust's shove: three
;                     squares west, to 11,18 - toward 0,0.
;   --- home ---      the party gone to the far corner, 12 seconds: the
;                     skeleton walks back EAST to 14,18 (it walked on toward
;                     the corner, west and north), never having noticed the
;                     party; then savemap, and the judge reads eval_arena.ent.
;   --- authored ---  crypt2, where the judge planted a skeleton at 5,6 with
;                     leashfrom=6,6: its anchor is the authored 6,6. The
;                     making now sets the spawn as the default, so the record's
;                     leashfrom= must still be read after it and win.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
echo --- checked ---
validate
echo --- made ---
editor place monsters skeleton 16 18
spawn skeleton 20 18 s 1 up
leash
echo --- moved ---
editor move 16 18 14 18
leash
mappage close
save leashtest
goto crypt1
goto eval_arena
echo --- returned ---
leash
load leashtest
echo --- loaded ---
leash
echo --- leashed ---
editor erase 12 1
editor erase 12 6
editor erase 25 7
editor erase 23 9
editor erase 24 10
editor erase 13 13
editor erase 20 18
editor inspect 14 18
editor inspector leash 1
editor inspector save
leash
mappage close
tp 15 18
face w
castsvc shove 3
echo --- shoved ---
leash
tp 24 2
step 12
echo --- home ---
leash
monsters
savemap
goto crypt2
echo --- authored ---
leash
echo --- end ---
